# Mix: a double tap on a track's black key solos it and the solo stays, let go (any page); a tap ends it and the
# mutes come back. A hold still adds a track while held; a mute changed elsewhere ends the solo first. The Mix page's
# mutes and solo are the mixer's (the audio: amute, the engine's; the scene's note mutes stay as they are)
wait 300
tap GLO
expect amute 0
tapkey b2
wait 100
tapkey b2
wait 40
expect amute 251
expect solo 4
expect mute 0
wait 1200
expect amute 251
shot mix_solo_latched.png
# a hold adds track 5 while held; let go, track 3 still alone
key b4 down
wait 900
expect amute 235
key b4 up
wait 40
expect amute 251
# a tap: the solo ends
tapkey b5
wait 400
expect amute 0
expect solo 0
# track 2 muted, then track 4 double tapped: the first tap's mute undone, track 2's kept to go back to
tapkey b1
wait 400
expect amute 2
expect mix2 1
tapkey b3
wait 100
tapkey b3
wait 40
expect amute 247
expect mix4 0
expect mix2 1
# another track double tapped while soloed: it alone
tapkey b6
wait 100
tapkey b6
wait 40
expect amute 191
tapkey b6
wait 400
expect amute 2
expect mute 0
# a note-muted track (Arrange's black keys: the scene's) still shows its steps on its meter, in grey (an empty muted
# track none); Mix's crossed speaker on track 2 (muted at the mixer)
notes 2 1 1 1 100 60
notes 2 1 5 1 100 62
notes 2 1 9 1 100 64
notes 2 1 13 1 100 65
tap HOME
expect page Arrange
tapkey b1
tapkey b3
wait 40
expect mute 10
tap GLO
expect page Mix
tapkey b1
wait 400
expect mix2 0
tap PLAY
wait 600
expect mute 10
expect amute 0
wait 900
shot mix_muted_meter.png
tap PLAY
